// boxcxx — <__bits/version_mutex>
//
// The one feature-test macro [version.syn] gives <mutex>: P0156R2's
// scoped_lock. Split into a leaf for the same [support.limits.general]
// per-header reason as every other version_* file -- see
// <__bits/version_any> for the full explanation.
//
// It was withheld because scoped_lock had no `mutex_type`: the variadic
// primary covered the one-mutex case through `if constexpr`, which locks
// correctly but cannot carry a conditional typedef. Ф31e-d supplied it from
// a base, which is what [thread.lock.scoped] describes -- a member present
// "only if sizeof...(MutexTypes) == 1" -- rather than a second class body.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

#if (defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL) || defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_scoped_lock)) && \
    !defined(__cpp_lib_scoped_lock)
#  define __cpp_lib_scoped_lock 201703L
#endif
#undef BOXCXX_OWNS_scoped_lock
